ource_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_chromadb", "label": "ChromaDB (vector_database/ store)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_ollama", "label": "Ollama local AI server (:11434)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_account_model", "label": "Account (DB model)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_emailaccount_model", "label": "EmailAccount (DB model)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_emailtoken_model", "label": "EmailToken (DB model)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_email_model", "label": "Email (DB model)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_chromadb_mails_collection", "label": "ChromaDB 'mails' collection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_single_writer_ownership", "label": "Single-writer resource ownership pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each Python service is the sole owner of exactly one resource domain (Database owns gmail_agent.db, Accounts owns credentials/OAuth, User_data owns Gmail/Calendar clients, Vector DB owns Chroma, MCP owns LLM orchestration) so ownership boundaries stay unambiguous and only the Gateway is publicly reachable, keeping rate-limit checks and business logic out of the Gateway."}, {"id": "readme_go_writes_sqlite_directly", "label": "Go sync server writes straight to SQLite (documented exception)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Database service is the sole Python owner of gmail_agent.db, but the Go sync server on :8001 opens the same file directly to INSERT into emails and SELECT email_tokens. This is a deliberate, documented exception to single-writer ownership, kept because rewriting the Go writer was out of scope; it also makes backend/go-server/ immovable since its DBPath is a relative path."}, {"id": "readme_interactive_oauth_in_request", "label": "Interactive OAuth runs inside a web request", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When a mailbox token cannot be refreshed, the credential ladder falls through to InstalledAppFlow.run_local_server(port=8080), an interactive browser flow started on the server inside an HTTP request. It is wrapped in run_in_threadpool and given a 120s Gateway timeout so it no longer blocks the event loop, but the fundamental shape (a hung re-auth degrades sign-in for everyone) is unchanged from before the refactor and was left as-is to preserve behavior."}, {"id": "readme_ratelimiter_fail_open_note", "label": "Rate limiter fails open when unavailable", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When running Python services without the Go rate limiter, the Python rate-limiter client fails open gracefully so requests proceed without disruption rather than blocking all traffic on an optional dependency."}, {"id": "readme_new_emails_semantics", "label": "'new_emails' means fetched, not newly saved", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GET /api/sync reports new_emails as the number of messages fetched, not the number newly written to the database. In the Go branch these numbers coincide; in the Python fallback branch the count diverges whenever a message_id repeats. Kept verbatim because it is pinned by two golden test files."}, {"id": "readme_x1_signup_account_takeover", "label": "X1: Sign-up account-takeover vector", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "POST /api/auth/signup with an email that already exists and any password returns a working session for somebody else's tenant. Deliberately left unfixed because fixing it changes observable behavior, which the behavior-preserving refactor was forbidden to do; tracked as its own ticket."}, {"id": "readme_x2_users_endpoint_leak", "label": "X2: GET /api/users leaks all tenants' accounts", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GET /api/users with no account_id returns every email account across all tenants; preserved verbatim to keep the golden suite green."}, {"id": "readme_x3_message_id_no_unique_constraint", "label": "X3: emails.message_id has no unique constraint", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Email lookups use filter_by(message_id=...).first(), so if two mailboxes cache the same message an arbitrary row wins; preserved as a pre-existing defect."}, {"id": "readme_x4_calendar_hardwired_account", "label": "X4: Calendar access hardwired to email account 1", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Calendar access is hardwired to email account 1 in three places; /api/calendar/status and /api/calendar/moodle silently fall back to it. Preserved verbatim rather than fixed."}, {"id": "readme_x5_thread_id_null", "label": "X5: thread_id is always NULL", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "thread_id is never populated by either sync path but is still returned by the email-details response; kept unchanged to preserve observable behavior."}, {"id": "readme_x6_invalid_slm_model_string", "label": "X6: invalid local SLM model string with trailing whitespace", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The local SLM model string is 'qwen3.8:27b-mlx  ' - not a valid model name and has trailing whitespace. Moved into config during the split but left verbatim rather than corrected."}, {"id": "readme_x7_duplicate_data_recorder", "label": "X7: duplicated dead data_recorder.py", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "data_recorder.py existed twice (under utilities/ and data_utils/), identical and imported by nothing; consolidated to one copy in backend/libs/common/ during the split, but it remains imported by nothing."}, {"id": "readme_x8_slm_response_commented_out", "label": "X8: /api/query local-SLM path commented out", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "/api/query has its local-SLM (slm_response) path commented out in favour of the OpenAI llm_response path; preserved as-is rather than re-enabled."}, {"id": "readme_x9_last_sync_time_process_local", "label": "X9: last_sync_time is process-local and stale", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The MCP last_sync_time context value is process-local, resets on restart, and is never updated by the public GET /api/sync; kept unchanged across the refactor."}, {"id": "readme_x10_blocking_calls_in_async_handlers", "label": "X10: blocking calls inside async def handlers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "requests.post to the Go server, googleapiclient calls, and limiter.check all block the event loop inside async handlers. The split added synchronous httpx credential fetches, the same class of problem, but this is accepted as no regression rather than fixed."}, {"id": "readme_golden_test_suite", "label": "Golden test suite (28 captured responses)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_e2e_test_rate_limiter", "label": "tests/e2e/test_rate_limiter.py", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_mcp_tool_registry", "label": "MCP tool registry (14 tools, 9 resources)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": nul